WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:04.240
Every guy wants to be a great husband.&nbsp;

00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:07.320
If you don't, then there's probably&nbsp;
something wrong with you and you will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.320 --> 00:00:10.920
never have a great marriage.
So how do you do it?&nbsp;

00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:18.920
How do you have a great marriage where&nbsp;
your wife treats you like a king?&nbsp;

00:00:18.920 --> 00:00:27.080
Well, she will automatically do&nbsp;
it if you treat her like a queen.&nbsp;

00:00:27.080 --> 00:00:29.960
Do you?
The Bible says in 1 Peter 3:7:

00:00:29.960 --> 00:00:30.360
[1 Peter 3:7]

00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:53.240
Now, there are a lot of things that we can talk&nbsp;
about when it comes to being a great husband, but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.240 --> 00:01:04.600
I want to focus in on five important things and&nbsp;
the first thing is: Treat your wife like a queen.&nbsp;

00:01:04.600 --> 00:01:08.120
It is so simple and yet so many&nbsp;
people do not realize this.&nbsp;

00:01:08.120 --> 00:01:16.360
So many men, that your actions create the&nbsp;
reactions from your wife and you can test it.&nbsp;

00:01:16.360 --> 00:01:25.280
For example, if you want her to make&nbsp;
you coffee in bed, start doing it first.&nbsp;

00:01:25.280 --> 00:01:30.240
All you got to do is treat her&nbsp;
the way you want her to treat you.&nbsp;

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:34.720
If you want more attention from her but&nbsp;
don't give her the attention she needs,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.720 --> 00:01:38.480
what do you think is going to happen ?
If you want her to make you delicious&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.480 --> 00:01:43.880
food sometimes but you never make food for&nbsp;
her or take care of your household chores,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.880 --> 00:01:48.080
then what do you think is going to happen?&nbsp;

00:01:48.080 --> 00:01:53.720
If you live with her in an understanding&nbsp;
way knowing what she needs - fulfilling&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.720 --> 00:01:59.840
it - then the chances are extremely high&nbsp;
that she will also fulfill your needs.&nbsp;

00:02:00.840 --> 00:02:04.720
But the husband is the leader&nbsp;
so you need to act first.&nbsp;

00:02:04.720 --> 00:02:10.920
I'll say it again - treat her like a&nbsp;
queen and she will treat you like a king.&nbsp;

00:02:10.920 --> 00:02:16.000
Wash her feet.
When was the last time you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:22.240
actually did something for your wife that she&nbsp;
really wanted or would like or is marriage for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.240 --> 00:02:27.080
you just about you... a selfish life?
The Bible says that the husband is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:32.280
the leader of the home just like&nbsp;
Jesus is the head of the church.&nbsp;

00:02:32.280 --> 00:02:39.560
What kind of leader was Jesus?
He led by example, by serving.&nbsp;

00:02:39.560 --> 00:02:45.840
He gave his life for the church and&nbsp;
he washed the feet of the disciples.

00:02:45.840 --> 00:02:47.800
[John 13:12-15]

00:03:15.440 --> 00:03:17.760
Now listen to this, very important part.

00:03:21.360 --> 00:03:22.440
[John 13:16]

00:03:33.440 --> 00:03:40.720
If you have to wash other people's feet - think&nbsp;
about them as more important than yourself.&nbsp;

00:03:40.720 --> 00:03:44.520
Then how more important is it&nbsp;
when it comes to your wife?&nbsp;

00:03:44.520 --> 00:03:52.160
The wife that God gave you to wash her feet.
Because remember, you are now one flesh.

00:03:52.160 --> 00:03:54.880
[Mark 10:7-9]

00:04:14.560 --> 00:04:24.720
If you lead your wife the way Jesus Christ leads&nbsp;
the church, then your wife will gladly follow you.&nbsp;

00:04:24.720 --> 00:04:29.280
Not because she feels that&nbsp;
she has to, but out of love.&nbsp;

00:04:29.280 --> 00:04:34.920
You're not the boss, you're the leader.
And you need to follow the example of Jesus.&nbsp;

00:04:34.920 --> 00:04:40.000
So you need to do what...?
You need to serve your wife.&nbsp;

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:47.360
Number three: Let go of your pride.
It's one of the biggest problems that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:47.360 --> 00:04:54.320
marriages experience is pride, especially&nbsp;
when it comes to the man in the house.&nbsp;

00:04:54.320 --> 00:04:59.360
When he is arrogant and full of pride.
Full of that self that Jesus says that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:59.360 --> 00:05:03.520
you have to deny yourself, pick&nbsp;
up your cross and follow Jesus.&nbsp;

00:05:03.520 --> 00:05:07.000
That is a true man.
A selfish man will never&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.000 --> 00:05:11.120
have a great marriage.
Listen to this verse.

00:05:11.120 --> 00:05:13.640
[Philippians 2:3-4]

00:05:35.800 --> 00:05:38.800
Now this does not mean that&nbsp;
you should let your wife walk&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:38.800 --> 00:05:44.120
all over you, because you are the leader.
You lead by example, by following Christ.&nbsp;

00:05:44.120 --> 00:05:46.640
By setting the example.
It means that you lead&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:46.640 --> 00:05:50.960
her according to God's Word.
That's how you set the example.&nbsp;

00:05:50.960 --> 00:05:57.560
According to this verse, you put yourself&nbsp;
in her shoes and understand what she needs&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:57.560 --> 00:06:04.560
from you and then give it to her and a lot of&nbsp;
times that requires you to sacrifice your own&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:04.560 --> 00:06:12.120
desires and to put her needs above your own.
And if you start to do that you will see that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:12.120 --> 00:06:20.240
she is starting to do the same and it creates&nbsp;
this amazing loving open caring relationship,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:20.240 --> 00:06:29.520
where you both are humble and willing to&nbsp;
support each other in whatever you need.&nbsp;

00:06:29.520 --> 00:06:35.520
Number four: Never put your wife above God.&nbsp;

00:06:35.520 --> 00:06:40.560
Always put God first in your life, above&nbsp;
yourself, above your wife, above your kids,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.560 --> 00:06:47.200
above everything else in your life.
If you do it, God will be with you.&nbsp;

00:06:47.200 --> 00:06:51.360
He will bless you in everything that you do.
He will take care of everything.

00:06:51.360 --> 00:06:52.360
[Romans 8:28]

00:07:01.320 --> 00:07:05.600
Especially when it comes to the big decisions.
Actually, all the decisions of your life.&nbsp;

00:07:05.600 --> 00:07:09.160
But especially decisions regarding your marriage,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:09.160 --> 00:07:17.320
your finances, your children,&nbsp;
career, your relationships.&nbsp;

00:07:17.320 --> 00:07:20.840
In all of it, you need to put&nbsp;
God first and follow His will.&nbsp;

00:07:20.840 --> 00:07:25.560
And then everything will&nbsp;
work out the way it should.

00:07:25.560 --> 00:07:27.680
[Matthew 6:31-32]

00:07:45.000 --> 00:07:47.080
These things - about clothing, drinking, food.&nbsp;

00:07:47.080 --> 00:07:51.720
These things are just examples of the&nbsp;
things that you worry about usually.&nbsp;

00:07:51.720 --> 00:07:57.640
God says that you don't need to worry about it.
He's your father and he will give you what you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:57.640 --> 00:08:01.800
need if you put Him first.
Listen to the next verse.

00:08:05.400 --> 00:08:06.040
[Matthew 6:33]

00:08:09.280 --> 00:08:13.280
That's the condition for the&nbsp;
promise that now follows.

00:08:14.200 --> 00:08:16.840
[Matthew 6:33]

00:08:21.080 --> 00:08:23.680
Of course, you need to include&nbsp;
your wife in all your decisions.&nbsp;

00:08:23.680 --> 00:08:30.240
Talk to her, ask her advice, because her role&nbsp;
as the wife is to support you, right? But your&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:30.240 --> 00:08:35.560
wife is not smarter than God.
You are not smarter than God.&nbsp;

00:08:35.560 --> 00:08:38.120
So you talk about these things.
Communication.&nbsp;

00:08:38.120 --> 00:08:42.040
So you know all your options.
You bring it to the feet of Jesus Christ.&nbsp;

00:08:42.040 --> 00:08:46.800
You pray about it and you ask Him,&nbsp;
alright, how do you want me to handle this?&nbsp;

00:08:46.800 --> 00:08:53.320
How do you want my wife to handle this?
How do you want us to act in this situation?

00:08:53.320 --> 00:08:55.720
[Proverbs 3:5-6]

00:09:11.240 --> 00:09:14.160
It doesn't say in all your&nbsp;
ways acknowledge yourself or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:14.160 --> 00:09:21.120
your wife or what everybody else tells you.
It says in all your ways, acknowledge Him.&nbsp;

00:09:21.120 --> 00:09:25.120
You as the leader of the home.
You have the responsibility to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:25.120 --> 00:09:28.160
follow God's will.
And then it says:

00:09:29.160 --> 00:09:29.960
[Proverbs 3:6]

00:09:33.800 --> 00:09:40.000
That's the blessing.
If your wife says one thing and God says another&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:40.000 --> 00:09:45.200
thing then you should not listen to your wife.
You should listen to God.&nbsp;

00:09:45.200 --> 00:09:51.280
For example, if your wife says let's go and buy&nbsp;
this car and you pray and know it is not God's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:51.280 --> 00:09:56.880
will to buy it, then don't do it.
She makes mistakes.&nbsp;

00:09:56.880 --> 00:10:02.240
You? You also make mistakes.
But God never makes any mistakes and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:02.240 --> 00:10:09.720
there's already so much in God's Word that He has&nbsp;
already revealed to us, how He wants us to live.&nbsp;

00:10:09.720 --> 00:10:14.360
And so if we follow it - if we walk&nbsp;
in His will - He will bless us.&nbsp;

00:10:14.360 --> 00:10:17.600
For example, the Bible says you&nbsp;
have to discipline your kids.&nbsp;

00:10:17.600 --> 00:10:21.800
If your wife doesn't want you to discipline your&nbsp;
kids and you listen to your wife and you don't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:21.800 --> 00:10:26.560
do it, God's not going to bless you.
The consequences of not obeying God.&nbsp;

00:10:26.560 --> 00:10:29.280
Because that is what sin is&nbsp;
... it is not obeying God.&nbsp;

00:10:29.280 --> 00:10:35.960
Sin in its essence is not following God's Word.
And the consequences of that is always bad.&nbsp;

00:10:35.960 --> 00:10:43.560
So what do you think is going to happen if you&nbsp;
don't discipline your kids in love and truth?&nbsp;

00:10:43.560 --> 00:10:48.400
Then your children will not respect you&nbsp;
and will grow up into selfish adults who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:48.400 --> 00:10:54.720
think they always get what they want, when they&nbsp;
want, no matter what they do, even if it's bad.&nbsp;

00:10:54.720 --> 00:10:57.880
Evil.
There's no consequences.&nbsp;

00:10:57.880 --> 00:11:01.480
And they always get away with it.
And doing that actually helps their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:01.480 --> 00:11:07.960
sinful flesh to grow even stronger.
And that's how criminals are created.&nbsp;

00:11:07.960 --> 00:11:12.440
Over the last few decades, parents have&nbsp;
been disciplining their kids less and less.&nbsp;

00:11:12.440 --> 00:11:16.520
They're not listening to the Word of God.
And what is the result?&nbsp;

00:11:16.520 --> 00:11:20.200
You can see this new generation&nbsp;
compared to our generation.&nbsp;

00:11:20.200 --> 00:11:28.640
They have a lot less respect for their parents.
They're very different and very selfish.&nbsp;

00:11:28.640 --> 00:11:33.160
And that is actually also a sign that&nbsp;
we're slowly moving towards the end times.

00:11:33.160 --> 00:11:35.240
[2 Timothy 3-5]

00:12:32.640 --> 00:12:38.000
Put God first in your life.
Discipline your children with love.&nbsp;

00:12:38.000 --> 00:12:42.120
If you do that while they're young, they&nbsp;
won't stray from it when they are older.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:42.120 --> 00:12:48.320
Folly is in the heart of a child, but&nbsp;
if you discipline him, it takes it out.&nbsp;

00:12:48.320 --> 00:12:52.880
Put God first in your marriage.
In everything that you do.&nbsp;

00:12:52.880 --> 00:12:58.040
It is God's Word that says that you have to&nbsp;
love your wife not when you feel like it.&nbsp;

00:12:58.040 --> 00:13:02.640
It's a command.
It's an act of your will, not just a feeling.&nbsp;

00:13:02.640 --> 00:13:06.320
The feeling, a lot of people focus on&nbsp;
that kind of love, is the eros love.&nbsp;

00:13:06.320 --> 00:13:09.440
Sexual love.
The attraction love.&nbsp;

00:13:09.440 --> 00:13:15.640
There's also agape love, which is the&nbsp;
unconditional love that God has for us.&nbsp;

00:13:15.640 --> 00:13:18.080
That's the love that you also&nbsp;
have to have for your wife,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:18.080 --> 00:13:21.040
to love her even when you don't feel like it.

00:13:21.040 --> 00:13:23.960
[Ephesians 5:25]

00:13:39.120 --> 00:13:43.680
True peace and joy come only from God.
Not from your wife.&nbsp;

00:13:43.680 --> 00:13:49.600
Your wife helps, but that kind of peace that&nbsp;
surpasses all understanding and that joy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:49.600 --> 00:13:53.240
even in trials and tribulations&nbsp;
- that can come only from God.&nbsp;

00:13:53.240 --> 00:13:57.680
And you need to understand this because&nbsp;
there are a lot of couples out there,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:57.680 --> 00:14:01.000
they blame their partners because&nbsp;
they don't have a good life,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:01.000 --> 00:14:07.160
instead of taking responsibility for&nbsp;
your own life and looking to Christ.

00:14:07.160 --> 00:14:11.720
Your wife is not responsible&nbsp;
for how you feel all the time.&nbsp;

00:14:11.720 --> 00:14:13.720
She does help you to have a great life,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:13.720 --> 00:14:19.760
but it is your responsibility and you need&nbsp;
to look to God to get that fire within you.

00:14:19.760 --> 00:14:21.640
[John 14:27]

00:14:39.200 --> 00:14:43.160
You always get your purpose, that fire,&nbsp;
purpose, peace, fulfillment ... everything&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:43.160 --> 00:14:48.880
that you need, you can get from Jesus Christ.
Don't look to it at your wife all the time and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:48.880 --> 00:14:52.520
expect her to give you everything the whole time.
You're going to burn her out.&nbsp;

00:14:52.520 --> 00:14:56.800
You're going to be too clingy&nbsp;
and she will get tired of it.&nbsp;

00:14:56.800 --> 00:14:59.520
I'll say it again.
True peace and joy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:59.520 --> 00:15:07.600
come only from God and not from temporary&nbsp;
worldly things including people and your wife.

00:15:07.600 --> 00:15:09.480
[Philippians 4:6]

00:15:23.240 --> 00:15:26.440
In other words, lean on God.
Have a good relationship with God.&nbsp;

00:15:26.440 --> 00:15:31.280
Talk to him all the time.
This is where you get the peace&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:31.280 --> 00:15:34.280
that surpasses all understanding.
Which it says in the next verse.

00:15:38.600 --> 00:15:41.560
[Phillippians 4:7]

00:15:47.000 --> 00:15:53.360
You know, a lot of men complain about their wives.
They say things like she should be less grumpy.&nbsp;

00:15:53.360 --> 00:15:56.240
She should be more thankful&nbsp;
to me for working hard.&nbsp;

00:15:56.240 --> 00:16:01.960
She should put on the clothes that I want her to.
She should stop nagging me all the time.&nbsp;

00:16:01.960 --> 00:16:07.840
She makes being a mom her main personality&nbsp;
trait, and she never gives me attention anymore.&nbsp;

00:16:07.840 --> 00:16:11.600
She should learn how to be&nbsp;
more hospitable to my family.&nbsp;

00:16:11.600 --> 00:16:17.560
She should do more in the house.

00:16:17.560 --> 00:16:19.080
She-she-she.&nbsp;

00:16:19.080 --> 00:16:22.960
It's always easier to look at&nbsp;
others and blame others, right?&nbsp;

00:16:22.960 --> 00:16:28.520
While some of those things might be true and&nbsp;
she might improve on it based on God's Word.&nbsp;

00:16:29.680 --> 00:16:36.320
Did it ever occur to you that maybe some of those&nbsp;
things that she's doing is a result a reaction?&nbsp;

00:16:36.320 --> 00:16:42.600
Reactions, maybe more, because of YOUR actions?
How YOU are in the house.&nbsp;

00:16:42.600 --> 00:16:49.120
She might be tired of giving and giving and&nbsp;
giving and not really receiving anything from you.&nbsp;

00:16:49.120 --> 00:16:57.080
The things that she really needs.
And she's just human and humans are not perfect.&nbsp;

00:16:57.080 --> 00:17:02.480
Are you giving your wife what&nbsp;
she needs according to the Bible?

00:17:02.480 --> 00:17:04.760
[1 Peter 3:7]

00:17:24.080 --> 00:17:27.880
This is so serious to God that He's&nbsp;
basically saying that if you don't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:27.880 --> 00:17:35.440
treat your wife in an understanding way, the&nbsp;
way you should according to the Word of God,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:35.440 --> 00:17:40.320
then your prayers will be hindered.
You might be busy with religious things.&nbsp;

00:17:40.320 --> 00:17:43.240
You might even preach in the church.
You might do your Bible studies and do all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:43.240 --> 00:17:51.320
these religious things, while they actually mean&nbsp;
nothing, because your prayers that's hindered.&nbsp;

00:17:51.320 --> 00:17:56.800
Because back home you and your&nbsp;
relationship with your wife is not good.&nbsp;

00:17:56.800 --> 00:18:02.440
You're not treating her the way you should.
Some of you are too harsh with the wife&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:02.440 --> 00:18:08.080
that God gave you.
This is serious.

00:18:08.080 --> 00:18:09.200
[Colossians 3:19]

00:18:21.000 --> 00:18:26.040
Guys, we need to understand this.
If we don't treat our wives right, if we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:26.040 --> 00:18:34.800
don't lead them according to God's Word, then our&nbsp;
wives, they have full right to hold us accountable&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:34.800 --> 00:18:39.440
because they need to support us, right?
And that means when we stray from the path, they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:39.440 --> 00:18:47.600
always put God first, right? When we stray they&nbsp;
have the right to say, hey, come back on the path.&nbsp;

00:18:47.600 --> 00:18:55.040
That means they don't have to listen to you if you&nbsp;
say things that are not in line with scripture.&nbsp;

00:18:55.040 --> 00:19:00.920
But if you do say things to her - if you&nbsp;
do lead according to scripture - then she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:00.920 --> 00:19:05.680
needs to listen to you because then&nbsp;
she's just obeying scripture, right?

00:19:05.680 --> 00:19:07.080
[Ephesians 5:22]

00:19:12.440 --> 00:19:14.720
As to the Lord.
This is amazing, right?&nbsp;

00:19:14.720 --> 00:19:20.840
Because this is an example of how our relationship&nbsp;
is - true believers with Christ, right?&nbsp;

00:19:20.840 --> 00:19:23.360
The church.
And Christ, how He came to serve.&nbsp;

00:19:23.360 --> 00:19:26.920
How He loves us.
And so this is as Paul&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:26.920 --> 00:19:29.560
puts it - it is profound.
You get it?&nbsp;

00:19:29.560 --> 00:19:35.320
It means that you never lead your&nbsp;
wife - your household - in the flesh.&nbsp;

00:19:35.320 --> 00:19:39.960
You as John, Peter, David - you&nbsp;
don't lead it as you want to.&nbsp;

00:19:39.960 --> 00:19:46.080
You lead your wife and your&nbsp;
children as Christ leads the church.&nbsp;

00:19:46.080 --> 00:19:51.480
So don't lead them in the soul level - your own&nbsp;
intellect - your own emotions - your own will.&nbsp;

00:19:51.480 --> 00:19:54.760
We're going to do this.
No, you lead them through&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:54.760 --> 00:20:02.400
the Spirit as Christ leads the church in truth.
In love, in, oh there's so much beauty in that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:02.400 --> 00:20:08.800
kind of relationship, that kind of leadership.
And that includes forgiving each other as well.&nbsp;

00:20:08.800 --> 00:20:12.800
As Christ forgave you, you&nbsp;
also need to forgive your wife.

00:20:12.800 --> 00:20:14.400
[Ephesians 4:32]

00:20:25.360 --> 00:20:28.360
Marriage is awesome.
One of the best things&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:28.360 --> 00:20:36.040
you will ever experience in this life.
If God is in the center, and if all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:36.040 --> 00:20:44.240
these four types of love is in it as well.
Storge - family love, philia - friendship&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:44.240 --> 00:20:56.600
love, eros- sexual attraction love, and&nbsp;
agape - unconditional sacrificial love.&nbsp;

00:20:56.600 --> 00:21:01.400
A marriage is the only relationship&nbsp;
with these four types of love in it.&nbsp;

00:21:01.400 --> 00:21:06.280
And agape is the most important because&nbsp;
that is unconditional sacrificial love.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:06.280 --> 00:21:12.920
You sacrifice your own life and you put&nbsp;
your wife - her needs - above your own.&nbsp;

00:21:12.920 --> 00:21:18.200
That's the kind of love where&nbsp;
you have an amazing marriage.&nbsp;

00:21:18.200 --> 00:21:22.800
This is where you choose to always&nbsp;
love your wife no matter what,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:22.800 --> 00:21:27.560
because it is not a feeling, it is&nbsp;
an act of your will, and you have no&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:27.560 --> 00:21:33.920
excuses because if you are a true reborn&nbsp;
Christian, you have God's Spirit in you.&nbsp;

00:21:33.920 --> 00:21:41.520
That means you can produce the fruit&nbsp;
of the Spirit and one of it is love.

00:21:41.520 --> 00:21:43.480
[Galatians 5:22]

00:22:03.760 --> 00:22:08.680
Now, go and produce this fruit in your marriage.
Love your wife the right way.&nbsp;

00:22:08.680 --> 00:22:13.360
Lead your wife the right way.
And be a great husband.&nbsp;

00:22:13.360 --> 00:22:15.640
And if you haven't subscribed&nbsp;
yet, then please subscribe.&nbsp;

00:22:15.640 --> 00:22:21.000
